# 🏛 CAPSTONE — LexRAG-BR (Legal Document Analyzer)

#estudos #ai-mermaid #portfolio #capstone #status-ativo

> Source: item 4 of Month 12 in [[Projetos Portfolio IA]] (Analisador de documentos legais).
> Goal: one repo that touches every month of [[AI Mermaid Plano]], ends in a live demo, and doubles as content for [[GitHub Monetização]].

## 1. Why this project

| Criterion | Fit |
|---|---|
| Curriculum coverage | Months 1–12 + Extra (see §4) |
| Existing edge | Prior large-scale document pipeline experience (see [[Banco de Numeros]]) |
| Gap closing | Hits 🚨 Math/Stats, ⚠️ ML, ⏳ DL, MLOps, Transformers, Transfer Learning, NLP/LLMs, RAG |
| Portfolio | Quarto write-up + live demo + GitHub repo ([[Fontes de Dados Portfolio]]) |
| Research link | Text/sequence analysis → bridge to PhD direction ([[Literatura Pesquisa PhD]]) |
| Monetization | Tutorial per stage; template/roadmap product |

## 2. Problem statement

Given Brazilian public court decisions, build a system that:
1. **Classifies** each decision (area of law, and outcome if labeled).
2. **Retrieves** relevant precedents for a natural-language question.
3. **Answers with citations** (case number + passage), refusing when evidence is missing.

Data: public decisions/legislation from dados.gov.br or basedosdados.org (verify licence and schema before ingesting). Public data only, no client material.

## 3. Architecture

| # | Stage | Tools | Output |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | Ingest | Python, requests/pandas | Raw corpus (`data/raw`) |
| 2 | Store | SQLite → Postgres, SQL | Tables: `decisions`, `chunks`, `labels` |
| 3 | EDA | Pandas, Matplotlib, Quarto | Length/class distributions, missingness, leakage check |
| 4 | Stats | SciPy/statsmodels | Class-imbalance tests, CIs on all metrics |
| 5 | Baseline ML | TF-IDF + LogReg/LinearSVC (Scikit-Learn) | Baseline F1 |
| 6 | Deep learning | PyTorch, BERTimbau fine-tune | Transfer-learning classifier |
| 7 | Chunk + embed | Sentence-Transformers (multilingual) | Vectors |
| 8 | Vector DB | Faiss (local) → Qdrant/Milvus (stretch) | Index + metadata filters |
| 9 | RAG | LangChain or plain Python, Claude API | Cited answers + refusal rule |
| 10 | Evaluation | Hit@k, MRR, faithfulness, answer relevance | `eval/report.md` |
| 11 | Serve | FastAPI + Streamlit | `/classify`, `/ask` |
| 12 | MLOps | MLflow, Docker, GitHub Actions, DVC | Tracked runs, CI, container |
| 13 | Deploy + publish | HF Spaces/Render, Quarto | Live demo + case study |

