## 5. Plan (8 sprints, 1 week each)

| Sprint | Focus | Done when |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | Repo, data source, ingestion, SQL schema | ≥ 10k docs in DB, README v0 |
| 2 | EDA + stats | Quarto EDA published, label strategy fixed |
| 3 | Baseline ML | Cross-validated baseline + MLflow run |
| 4 | Transformer fine-tune | Beats baseline, significance test reported |
| 5 | Chunking, embeddings, vector index | Hit@5 measured on 50 hand-written queries |
| 6 | RAG + citations + refusal | Faithfulness check on 50 queries |
| 7 | API, UI, Docker, CI | `docker compose up` runs everything |
| 8 | Deploy, write-up, content | Live URL + case study + 3 tutorials |

## 6. Repo structure

```
lexrag-br/
├── data/            # raw/ processed/ (DVC-tracked, not in git)
├── notebooks/       # 01_eda, 02_baseline, 03_finetune, 04_retrieval
├── src/
│   ├── ingest/  db/  features/  models/  retrieval/  rag/  api/
├── eval/            # queries.jsonl, metrics, report.md
├── app/             # Streamlit UI
├── tests/
├── docker/  .github/workflows/
├── quarto/          # portfolio case study
└── README.md        # problem, architecture diagram, results table, demo link
```

## 7. Evaluation targets

| Component | Metric | Target |
|---|---|---|
| Baseline classifier | Macro-F1 | Reported with CI |
| Fine-tuned model | Macro-F1 | > baseline, p < 0.05 |
| Retrieval | Hit@5 / MRR | Hit@5 ≥ 0.80 on own query set |
| RAG answers | Faithfulness (manual, 50 q) | ≥ 90% supported by cited passage |
| Refusal | Correct "no evidence" rate | Tested on 20 out-of-corpus questions |
| Ops | Cold start, latency p95 | Documented |

## 8. Risks

| Risk | Mitigation |
|---|---|
| Labels weak or missing | Start with area-of-law from metadata; hand-label a 300-doc gold set |
| Long documents | Section-aware chunking + overlap; test chunk sizes |
| Hallucinated citations | Return only retrieved IDs; verify quotes against source |
| Scope creep | Faiss first; Qdrant/Milvus and multi-agent are stretch only |
| Legal advice misuse | Disclaimer in UI: research tool, not legal advice |

